orecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 61% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"353.236\" cy=\"159.04999999999998\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"377.3925373134328\" cy=\"115.7910447761194\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 95%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"393.8014084507041\" cy=\"130.7887323943662\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 87% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 206 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.848640776699\" cy=\"63.94174757281553\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(61%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Douala the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.04) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.62).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>168</td><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'>-0.620</td><td class='num'>32.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>-0.252</td><td class='num'>26.3%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>161</td><td class='num'>93%</td><td class='num'>-0.219</td><td class='num'>8.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>74%</td><td class='num'>0.042</td><td class='num'>16.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":4.04827,"lon":9.70428,"n":687,"n_cities":213,"name":"Douala","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.46200000000000013,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.2834782608695652,"n":69,"obs":0.18840579710144928,"sig":false},{"hi":0.61,"lo":0.46200000000000013,"mean":0.5353225806451614,"n":62,"obs":0.25806451612903225,"sig":true},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.61,"mean":0.6673529411764705,"n":68,"obs":0.39705882352941174,"sig":true},{"hi":0.8,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.76,"n":64,"obs":0.546875,"sig":true},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.8,"mean":0.834,"n":80,"obs":0.6125,"sig":true},{"hi":0.93,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9022388059701492,"n":67,"obs":0.7313432835820896,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9720000000000004,"lo":0.93,"mean":0.9485915492957744,"n":71,"obs":0.6901408450704225,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9720000000000004,"mean":0.9967475728155339,"n":206,"obs":0.8737864077669902,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.0,"provisional":false,"rank":181,"rank_hi":189.02499999999998,"rank_lo":160.0,"reliability":0.0393066707980526,"resolution":0.05685200878690328,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"douala","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Douala"}